AB  - This review aims at RCT's of psychedelics used in the treatment of depression and PTSD. Psilocybin has shown an antidepressant effect in cancer patients that was  sustained at 6- and 12-months follow-up. The effect of psilocybin was comparable  to escitalopram in one study. Ketamine has shown effect for the treatment of  resistant depression. Phase 2 and 3 trials have shown the effect of MDMA on PTSD.  No serious adverse events were reported in controlled settings, but larger  studies are needed to establish safety and long-term effects.
